# `genesis/data/rakia` — observed capacity governance

The aggregate binding reads typed `cluster.ratifications` in `compute-capacity.json`: only CPU
limits may exceed allocatable up to the ratified percentage; requests reserve and memory is
incompressible. A ledger older than 30 days refers for refresh without an aggregate-capacity ask,
retaining the underlying violations in the message. Run `k8s-bridge observe` to promote a fresh
cluster observation; the command lands with Station 2/3b.
